reviews.review:
This game is everything I was expecting: the worldbuilding, the art and the music are beautiful and go very well togheter. 

The main mechanics of the game are learning the songs and taking care of your garden and they are super fun. Basically, you do magic by playing song and uses magic to take care of your garden. There are lots of crops, and they don't die when the season changes.The minigames are super fun and making potions will also help on your garden. The fishing is a a rythm minigame that diferentiate the game from other farm-sims I played. 

The story seems like it came straight up from a children's fantasy book, it is clear that the writer had lot of good references and managed to do something unique with it. This, however, doesn't mean the game fails to touch adult themes and struggles, but it does it on a sensible and wholesome way. So do not fear it, the game will make you feel good after playing it. The ending is really good.

As any other farming sim this game has festivals and they are very creative, my favorites were the spring and the winter ones. 

I think anyone can try this game and have fun, but now I would like to make some points so you can make an informed decision:

- This game is more focused on the rpg and adventure side of it. It has everything any farm sim has, but I would say that its mechanics are intended to support the main story plot. The post game is more intended so you can complete any pending quests;
- There is no stress relative to time. The game pauses its clock when an important event will occur and also at the end of the night. Important events will be added to your calendar automatically, so it is very pratical. I was skeptical with this feature before playing (I actually like the time pressure from games like stardew valley), but I really enjoyed it at the end. You can build everything you want and is possible to acomplish anything that you missed in the end of the day;
- The rhythm mechanics are essential, but if you have any dificulty with ot there are acessibility options on the main menu. This is also valid for the potion minigame; 
- The quests of the game are fun and are not simple fetch quests, you will need to explore all mechanics in the game in order to complete the quests. New quests appear on every season and some will take more then one season to acomplished; Great level design;
- The story and the world of the game is very imersive. The art and music direction are great.


I had tons of fun playing the game, and problably will play it again very soon!
